# Security headers for nazbyte.com (Cloudflare Pages reads this file at deploy time)
# Docs: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# VERIFIED against the actual pages in this repo on 2026-10-03:
#   - NO executable inline <script> remains. The two that existed (feedback.html's form engine,
#     index.html's nav + enquiry form) were extracted to /assets/feedback.js and
#     /assets/home.js, so script-src carries NO 'unsafe-inline'. Mozilla Observatory penalises
#     'unsafe-inline' in script-src ONLY - that was the last remaining -20.
#   - <script type="application/ld+json"> blocks stay inline on purpose: they are data, not
#     executable code, so script-src does not apply to them and crawlers must find them in the HTML.
#   - style-src still needs 'unsafe-inline': 4 <style> blocks + 34 style="" attributes remain.
#     Observatory does NOT check style-src, so this costs no points.
#   - the ONLY external network destination from JS is script.google.com (tester feedback form)
#   - blob: is used by the image compressor for previews/downloads
#   - Cloudflare Web Analytics injects static.cloudflareinsights.com/beacon.min.js into every
#     response (zone setting, not this repo) - it must stay allowed in script-src + connect-src,
#     otherwise the analytics silently stop recording.
#   - no external fonts, no CDNs
#
# HSTS IS SET HERE (as an origin response header) rather than via the zone toggle, so that it is
# version-controlled with the site and reproducible. IMPORTANT: do NOT also enable the dashboard
# toggle (SSL/TLS -> Edge Certificates -> HSTS) - two HSTS headers would be malformed and browsers
# reject them. Pick one place; this is it. `preload` is deliberately omitted: it is a near-permanent
# commitment, and it can be added later once the domain has been stable for a while.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), autoplay=(), camera=(), display-capture=(), encrypted-media=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), midi=(), payment=(), picture-in-picture=(), publickey-credentials-get=(), screen-wake-lock=(), usb=(), xr-spatial-tracking=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://script.google.com https://cloudflareinsights.com; frame-src 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self' https://script.google.com; object-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests

# ---- Ad-carrying pages: /tools/* only (APPROVED by Anila, 2026-10-03) ----
# AdSense cannot serve under the strict /* policy above: script-src has no
# 'unsafe-inline' (the adsbygoogle push snippet), frame-src is 'self' (ad
# iframes) and default-src 'self' cascades to img-src/connect-src (creatives and
# beacons). Google documents a strict nonce-based policy as the supported route,
# but a static file on Pages cannot carry a per-response random nonce without
# adding a Pages Function, so the approved resolution is: permissive on the ad
# pages, strict everywhere else. Everything else is kept as tight as before.
# NO 'strict-dynamic' here on purpose - with no nonce on the page it would make
# the host allowlist be ignored. NO COEP anywhere - it blocks AdSense iframes.
#
# PHASE 1 (this commit): Report-Only, so violations show up in the console
# without blocking anything, while the enforced /* policy stays as it was.
# PHASE 2 (next commit): promote to the enforced header once the report is clean.
/tools/*
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'unsafe-eval' https:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https:; frame-src 'self' https:; frame-ancestors 'self'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self' https://script.google.com; object-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests

# Admin/tester pages: keep them out of search engines at the header level too,
# independent of the meta robots tag inside the file.
/feedback.html
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow, noarchive

/feedback
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow, noarchive
